(5032, 'mw_polylang_strings_plugins_data', 'a:1:{s:7:\"strings\";a:7545:{i:0;s:51:\"Your WordPress version is too old for XML Sitemaps.\";i:1;s:35:\"XML Sitemap Generator for WordPress\";i:2;s:90:\"The old files could NOT be deleted. Please use an FTP program and delete them by yourself.\";i:3;s:40:\"The old files were successfully deleted.\";i:4;s:40:\"Notify Search Engines about all sitemaps\";i:5;s:130:\"The plugin is notifying the selected search engines about your main sitemap and all sub-sitemaps. This might take a minute or two.\";i:6;s:9:\"All done!\";i:7;s:51:\"Ping was executed, please see below for the result.\";i:8;s:126:\"Thank you very much for your donation. You help me to continue support and development of this plugin and other free software!\";i:9;s:16:\"Hide this notice\";i:10;s:24:\"Sure, but I already did!\";i:11;s:40:\"No thanks, please don\\\'t bug me anymore!\";i:12;s:24:\"Don\\\'t show this anymore\";i:13;s:15:\"Plugin Homepage\";i:14;s:17:\"Suggest a Feature\";i:15;s:10:\"Help / FAQ\";i:16;s:11:\"Notify List\";i:17;s:13:\"Support Forum\";i:18;s:12:\"Report a Bug\";i:19;s:14:\"translator_url\";i:20;s:15:\"translator_name\";i:21;s:15:\"Webmaster Tools\";i:22;s:14:\"Webmaster Blog\";i:23;s:11:\"Search Blog\";i:24;s:21:\"Webmaster Center Blog\";i:25;s:17:\"Sitemaps Protocol\";i:26;s:21:\"Official Sitemaps FAQ\";i:27;s:15:\"My Sitemaps FAQ\";i:28;s:41:\"Search engines haven\\\'t been notified yet\";i:29;s:28:\"Recent Support Topics / News\";i:30;s:7:\"Disable\";i:31;s:69:\"No support topics available or an error occurred while fetching them.\";i:32;s:111:\"Support Topics have been disabled. Enable them to see useful information regarding this plugin. No Ads or Spam!\";i:33;s:6:\"Enable\";i:34;s:92:\"Search engines haven\\\'t been notified yet. Write a post to let them know about your sitemap.\";i:35;s:145:\"Since you are using Nginx as your web-server, please configure the following rewrite rules in case you get 404 Not Found errors for your sitemap:\";i:36;s:20:\"Update notification:\";i:37;s:10:\"Learn more\";i:38;s:40:\"Notify Google about updates of your site\";i:39;s:65:\"Notify Bing (formerly MSN Live Search) about updates of your site\";i:40;s:47:\"Add sitemap URL to the virtual robots.txt file.\";i:41;s:115:\"The virtual robots.txt generated by WordPress is used. A real robots.txt file must NOT exist in the site directory!\";i:42;s:17:\"Advanced options:\";i:43;s:36:\"Try to increase the memory limit to:\";i:44;s:44:\"Try to increase the execution time limit to:\";i:45;s:79:\"Try to automatically compress the sitemap if the requesting client supports it.\";i:46;s:82:\"Disable this option if you get garbled content or encoding errors in your sitemap.\";i:47;s:26:\"Include a XSLT stylesheet:\";i:48;s:38:\"Full or relative URL to your .xsl file\";i:49;s:11:\"Use default\";i:50;s:37:\"Override the base URL of the sitemap:\";i:51;s:126:\"Use this if your site is in a sub-directory, but you want the sitemap be located in the root. Requires .htaccess modification.\";i:52;s:30:\"Include sitemap in HTML format\";i:53;s:46:\"(The required PHP XSL Module is not installed)\";i:54;s:52:\"Allow anonymous statistics (no personal information)\";i:55;s:265:\"Here you can specify files or URLs which should be included in the sitemap, but do not belong to your Site/WordPress.<br />For example, if your domain is www.foo.com and your site is located on www.foo.com/site you might want to include your homepage at www.foo.com\";i:56;s:4:\"Note\";i:57;s:240:\"If your site is in a subdirectory and you want to add pages which are NOT in the site directory or beneath, you MUST place your sitemap file in the root directory (Look at the &quot;Location of your sitemap file&quot; section on this page)!\";i:58;s:15:\"URL to the page\";i:59;s:87:\"Enter the URL to the page. Examples: http://www.foo.com/index.html or www.foo.com/home \";i:60;s:8:\"Priority\";i:61;s:135:\"Choose the priority of the page relative to the other pages. For example, your homepage might have a higher priority than your imprint.\";i:62;s:12:\"Last Changed\";i:63;s:84:\"Enter the date of the last change as YYYY-MM-DD (2005-12-31 for example) (optional).\";i:64;s:16:\"Change Frequency\";i:65;s:1:\"#\";i:66;s:17:\"No pages defined.\";i:67;s:12:\"Add new page\";i:68;s:65:\"Please select how the priority of each post should be calculated:\";i:69;s:41:\"Do not use automatic priority calculation\";i:70;s:80:\"All posts will have the same priority which is defined in &quot;Priorities&quot;\";i:71;s:26:\"WordPress standard content\";i:72;s:16:\"Include homepage\";i:73;s:13:\"Include posts\";i:74;s:20:\"Include static pages\";i:75;s:18:\"Include categories\";i:76;s:16:\"Include archives\";i:77;s:20:\"Include author pages\";i:78;s:17:\"Include tag pages\";i:79;s:17:\"Custom taxonomies\";i:80;s:17:\"Custom post types\";i:81;s:15:\"Further options\";i:82;s:35:\"Include the last modification time.\";i:83;s:142:\"This is highly recommended and helps the search engines to know when your content has changed. This option affects <i>all</i> sitemap entries.\";i:84;s:19:\"Excluded categories\";i:85;s:13:\"Exclude posts\";i:86;s:37:\"Exclude the following posts or pages:\";i:87;s:31:\"List of IDs, separated by comma\";i:88;s:44:\"Child posts won\'t be excluded automatically!\";i:89;s:430:\"Please note that the value of this tag is considered a hint and not a command. Even though search engine crawlers consider this information when making decisions, they may crawl pages marked \"hourly\" less frequently than that, and they may crawl pages marked \"yearly\" more frequently than that. It is also likely that crawlers will periodically crawl pages marked \"never\" so that they can handle unexpected changes to those pages.\";i:90;s:8:\"Homepage\";i:91;s:5:\"Posts\";i:92;s:12:\"Static pages\";i:93;s:10:\"Categories\";i:94;s:73:\"The current archive of this month (Should be the same like your homepage)\";i:95;s:53:\"Older archives (Changes only 